# frules precedence

When several Forth rules are in context (Cursor attaches whole `.mdc` files by `globs`; cross-references do not auto-load), apply this order on conflict:

1. **`frules-dialect.mdc`** — chosen dialect (always applied).
2. **`forth-dialect-<name>.mdc`** — dialect syntax and idioms.
3. **`forth-portability.mdc`** — only when the project targets multiple Forths.
4. **`forth-anti-patterns.mdc`** — fix violations before adding more code.
5. **Other `forth-*.mdc`** — generic guidance (stack, style, control, factoring, defining, memory, io, strings, numeric, wordlists, debugging, oof, c-bindings, floating-point, meta).

Topic routing (pick the most specific file for the task):

| Task | Rule file |
|------|-----------|
| Stack order, manipulation, stack-effect design | `forth-stack.mdc` |
| Double/mixed precision, pictured numeric output | `forth-numeric.mdc` |
| if/loop/exit/recursion/flags, extended case | `forth-control.mdc` |
| CREATE/DOES>, defer, quotations, forward, alias | `forth-defining.mdc` |
| immediate, postpone, `[`/`]`, parsing/recognizers | `forth-meta.mdc` |
| variable, create, allot, move/cmove, alignment | `forth-memory.mdc` |
| open-file, CLI args, search paths | `forth-io.mdc` |
| s", c-addr u, xchars | `forth-strings.mdc` |
| FP stack, 1e, f~abs | `forth-floating-point.mdc` |
| Word lists, vocabularies, search order | `forth-wordlists.mdc` |
| see, ~~, depth-changes, inspection | `forth-debugging.mdc` |
| objects.fs classes (optional OOP) | `forth-oof.mdc` |
| cfunction, calling C libraries | `forth-c-bindings.mdc` |
| Gforth locals, require, try/endtry, structs | `forth-dialect-gforth.mdc` |
| Embedded port, missing wordsets, feature cost | `docs/FORTH-FEATURE-COMPLEXITY.md` (human reference) |

Do not repeat stack-tutorial material inside a defining-word edit.

If a needed topic is missing, prefer portable ANS words and ask to add `rules/forth-<topic>.mdc` from `sources/` (e.g. `gforth-manual/`, `gforth-manual-tutorial/`, `brodie-thinking-forth/`).
